#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:25
msgid ""
"Each object in the array `elements` denotes an installed package and has the "
"following fields:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:28
msgid ""
"`originalUrl`: The [flake reference](../../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-"
"flake.md) specified by the user at the time of installation (e.g. "
"`nixpkgs`). This is also the flake reference that will be used by `nix "
"profile upgrade`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:32
msgid "`uri`: The locked flake reference to which `originalUrl` resolved."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:34
msgid ""
"`attrPath`: The flake output attribute that provided this package. Note that "
"this is not necessarily the attribute that the user specified, but the one "
"resulting from applying the default attribute paths and prefixes; for "
"instance, `hello` might resolve to `packages.x86_64-linux.hello` and the "
"empty string to `packages.x86_64-linux.default`."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:41
msgid "`storePath`: The paths in the Nix store containing the package."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/files/manifest.json.md:43
msgid ""
"`active`: Whether the profile contains symlinks to the files of this "
"package. If set to false, the package is kept in the Nix store, but is not "
"\"visible\" in the profile's symlink tree."
msgstr ""
